  "query_preview": "..(This Evening Through Monday)\nIssued at 1244 PM MDT Mon Oct 19 2026\n\nCurrent upper air analysis shows southwest flow over the US as \ntrof deepens off the coast of the PNW. The CWA sits under mostly \nclear skies with sfc stations reporting temps in the upper 50s to \nlow 60s. \n\nBroad ridging will dominate the pattern through this week, \nkeeping conditions warm and dry. Weak shortwave and attendant cool\nfront will cross the region late Tuesday. Not expecting any \nprecip with this system but highs will be slightly cooler on \nWednesday. \n\nAmplifying upper ridge and breezy southerly flow will support \nmuch warmer temps on Thursday with highs in the upper 70s to low \n80s across much of the region. \n\nOur next chance at precip comes this weekend as trof pushes \nonshore over the western US. Deterministic and ensemble model \nsolutions diverge on the evolution of this trof as it pushes \neastward into the central US, leading to low forecast certainty on\ntiming and specific impacts from this system.",
